   "body": "<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe narrowly scoped handler preserves successful initialization and reports startup failures without introducing identified regressions.\n\n**No open issues** 🎉\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nThis PR addresses #344601 by adding error handling around VS Code CLI initialization, making startup failures clearer for users and automation.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Wraps NLS configuration, portable setup, ESM bootstrap, and CLI module loading in a single `try-catch`.\n- Logs a contextual fatal error and exits with code `1` when initialization fails.\n\nNo actionable defects were identified. Startup failure paths were not runtime-tested.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `src/​cli.ts` | Adds a bootstrap error handler with diagnostic logging and a nonzero exit code. |\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>",
